{
  "behaviorChanges": [
    "NOT WIP-SAFE for PR bodies. Two closing-reference checks now run at the prepush board gate and at `tautline merge`. A comma list after one keyword (`Resolves #A, #B`) is refused because GitHub honors the FIRST ref only and drops the rest silently -- RCA 2026-06-15, where #260 stayed open with nothing warning, since from GitHub's side nothing went wrong. A body with NO closing reference is refused because merging it auto-closes nothing: RCA 2026-07-18 control 3 measured 18 of 60 merged PRs in that state. The comma-list check cannot catch the second case -- zero refs yields zero list errors -- which is why both exist. A PREVIOUSLY GREEN PR BODY CAN NOW REFUSE; each message carries its own fix.",
    "The missing-reference check is exempt where the lane has already SAID the obligation does not apply: a non-development work profile, a recorded `board-binding` decision, or `allowRepoOnlyGoals` (0.64.0's sanctioned no-board-item path, honored rather than bypassed). All three resolve through ONE function both boundaries call, so prepush and merge cannot disagree about the same lane. None of them excuses a MALFORMED comma list: they answer whether a PR must bind an issue, never whether it may bind one wrongly. The `board-binding` exemption is scoped to a decision recorded NEWER than the branch's merge-base: an unscoped scan would mean using the documented escape hatch once exempted every later PR in the repository forever. GitHub's cross-repository form `owner/repo#123` is accepted, since it auto-closes exactly like `#123`. At merge both checks ride the existing `mergeGate.enforcement` switch (block / advise / off) and run BEFORE the `--override` decision record, so a refusal cannot leave the ledger claiming a break-glass for a merge nothing attempted.",
    "A `body` field ABSENT from the provider response is an unanswered question, not an empty body: both boundaries print `pr_closing_refs_warn:` and proceed rather than refuse a PR whose body was never read. An explicitly empty body still refuses."
  ],
